        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Manage Claw MCP server ownership",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- apply portable stdio and remote MCP declarations through OpenClaw's validated source-config writer\n- preserve `${ENV_VAR}` references and credential-free OAuth intent without storing server configuration in provenance\n- reuse exact existing declarations, distinguish Claw-created from independently owned config, and allow multiple Claws to share one exact server\n- expose MCP ownership and drift in status/export and remove only the final unchanged Claw-created declaration\n\n## Contract\n\n- dry-run shows each MCP command or URL before consent; apply rechecks source config and uses create-only writes\n- conflicting existing names block add; exact existing declarations are reused without mutation\n- provenance stores only agent, name, redacted digest, ownership class, and lifecycle status\n- pending writes reconcile deterministically against source config; unreadable source config fails planning before any cleanup\n- remove releases independently owned, shared, missing, failed, or operator-modified declarations and uses compare-before-unset for the final Claw-created declaration\n- cron jobs are disabled before MCP, agent, package, and workspace cleanup so scheduled work cannot race teardown\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.src.json ...`\n- focused Oxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors\n- generated Kysely schema verification and `git diff --check`\n- 91 focused unit, config, and CLI tests passed\n- 8 lifecycle E2E tests passed on current head, including add, status/remove, export, and consent flows\n- full Codex review against the stacked base: no actionable findings\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts\n✓ src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts (8 tests) 64953ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       8 passed (8)\n```\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102383 Gateway cron ownership\n- This PR: validated MCP source config, shared ownership, reconciliation, export, and safe removal\n- Next: #102427 projects the complete lifecycle state into doctor diagnostics\n\nMCP remains a separate stage because OpenClaw config, rather than the agent entry or Gateway scheduler, owns these declarations. The experimental CLI remains gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\n",
